# pull-health
- label: every real `import ssh` run writes one pull record per host to .pull-state.json in the hosts root — spec, lastAttemptAt, lastSuccessAt, ok, fetched, changed, skipped, failed, consecutiveFailures and the first line of the ssh/rsync error — a failed pull keeps the previous lastSuccessAt, --dry-run writes nothing, and the six-count summary (fact sshsm) is unchanged
  id: hubps
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'summary reports checked, fetched, imported, updated, skipped, and failed counts' test/bin/tracequest-ssh-import-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, hub-insights, cli, implemented]
- label: Insights names a machine whose pull fails by its configured host id only: `tracequest insights` text, the `insights --json` hub rows and the /insights machine panel carry no IP address, SSH destination or raw ssh/rsync error line — a failing row shows a short address-free reason such as 'connection timed out' — while ~/.tracequest/import-hosts, .pull-state.json and `tracequest import ssh` output keep the full address for whoever configures or debugs SSH
  id: hubna
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'names unreachable machines without their address' test/bin/insights-unreachable-hosts.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, hub-insights, cli, implemented]
- label: `tracequest insights` reports failing pulls in one short line after the machine rows — how many machines, their reasons, and that `tracequest import ssh` shows the ssh error — and no machine row repeats an error
  id: hubnw
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'warns once about failing pulls' test/bin/insights-unreachable-hosts.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, hub-insights, cli, implemented]

# scope
- label: Selecting, switching, or clearing a machine in Insights preserves the active filter expression and time range
  id: insms
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/browser/insights-machine-scope.playwright.test.js
  tags: [insights-machine-scope, implemented]

# examples
- label: each example session under an Insights error class (CLI `insights --json` and the /insights page) is labelled with that session's count for the whole class and how many of those errors carry the shown message — e.g. '27 errors of this class, 3 with this message; e.g. Error: …' — never a bare 'N×' before the message, so the class count cannot be read as the message's repeat count
  id: insexn
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/bin/insights-example-note.e2e.test.js
  tags: [spec, hub-insights, cli, ui, implemented]
